-- expect-refusal: is bound by another aggregate after the aggregate
-- examples/checks/agg-count-safety-5-refused-two-aggregates.rofl — B occurs
-- in no premise but the two aggregates, and in both. A variable is local to
-- an aggregate only when it occurs nowhere else in the rule, and the other
-- aggregate is elsewhere: so B is shared, bound by the second aggregate after
-- the first, which the load door refuses (docs/aggregates.md, "Scope"). Two
-- independent counts name their variables apart.
acs_two(N, M) :- N is count(B : acs_b(B, _)), M is count(B : acs_b(B, x)).
